{
  "abstract": "M. J. Plantholt and S. Shan, Edge coloring graphs with large minimum degree (arXiv:2105.05286), in Lean 4 / Mathlib. theorem_1_2 (Theorem 1.2): for every ε > 0 there is N such that a graph G on 2n vertices, n ≥ N, with δ(G) ≥ (1 + ε) n is Δ(G)-edge-colourable iff it has no Δ(G)-overfull subgraph (PlantholtShan.HasOverfullSubgraph, the definition of the registered plantholt-overfull-criterion entry restated in the challenge: an odd set of at least three vertices spanning more than Δ(G)(|S| − 1)/2 edges). theorem_1_3b (Theorem 1.3, Condition (b)): two vertices x ≠ y with d(x) = d(y) ≥ (1/2 + 3ε/2) n, all other vertices of degree Δ(G) ≥ (1 + ε) n and Δ(G) − δ(G) ≤ (1/2 − ε/2) n give χ′ = Δ for n ≥ N. theorem_1_3c (Condition (c)): Δ(G) − δ(G) ≥ n^{6/7}, at least n^{6/7} vertices of degree δ(G), at least n + 1 of degree Δ(G) and δ(G) ≥ (1 + ε) n give χ′ = Δ for n ≥ N (n^{6/7} as a real power). Condition (a) (regular graphs) is the registered asymptotic-one-factorization entry. lemma_2_11 (Lemma 2.11): a bipartite graph with sides of size n, all degrees at least t and at most t vertices of degree below n/2 has a perfect matching. Kept from version 1: hakimi (Theorem 2.5), hamiltonConnected_of_minDegree (Theorem 2.6, δ ≥ n/2 + 1) and exists_spanning_paths (Lemma 2.12). The thresholds N are explicit but huge (e.g. (2^60 q + 1)^21 with 1/q < ε) and not optimized. Two definitions (IsMultigraph, HasOverfullSubgraph). Seven statements.",
